media: h713-hdmirx: our own record cannot exist before we published one

The record at sig_phys is the HDMI source's until the display side
republishes the VidDec descriptor; from then on it carries the descriptor's
values, and 0136f recognises it by two of them - colour format 0 and a frame
rate of exactly 30.00 Hz. Those two are the descriptor's constants, but they
are not impossible for a real source, and a real source that had them would
have its rate thrown away and its geometry taken out of the comparison
(doku/128 section 3 item 4).

One more thing has to be true for the record to be ours: the descriptor must
have been written. The firmware cannot be echoing a publication that never
happened, so before the first one of a boot there is no own record at all,
whatever the record says. rx->desc_seen already carries exactly that, set by
h713_hdmirx_rearm() the moment the display side publishes, and it is now the
third term of the test.

That is the whole of the second distinguishing feature this driver can be
sure of, and the report of this package says so rather than pretending
otherwise: the 44 byte record carries no source field (AP3i section 1 lists
all eleven words), and where the firmware does not scale - every case on the
HY310 - the descriptor carries the ring, the ring IS the source, and the
geometry of the two records is the same. Whether the record's signal_id
differs between the two is not in any dump in this tree; reading the status
file once while the plane is on answers it, and if it does, the test can be
tightened again.

The frame rate taken off the flip pointers in that state is a second,
separate question and is left open on purpose. It is the panel's rate rather
than the source's whenever the plane is publishing (measured 21.09.2026:
720p50 came out as "720p60", 1080p24 as "1080p25"), and refusing it outright
would be the clean answer - except that a genuine 30.00 Hz source which
trips the two record fields above would then get -ENOLCK where it gets a
correct timing today, and 4K30 is exactly such a candidate. That trade needs
the device, not an argument; the package report names the check.

Follow-up to 0136f and 0136i, which stay byte-identical. The store in
h713_hdmirx_rearm() becomes a WRITE_ONCE because the flag is now read
outside that work.

Source: doku/128 section 3 item 4, umbau/work/T2/REPORT.txt sections 7.5 and
4e, umbau/re-apps/AP3i section 1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

